/target
# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace ships binaries, and DP-A2/DP-E8 require
# that a given commit rebuilds to the same bits with the same dependency set.

# The in-workspace C toolchain (TD-28, D-073). ~1 GB of third-party binaries,
# reproduced from the URL + SHA-256 recorded in docs/43 — never committed.
# It lives inside the repo so DP-S5 holds: no global install, no PATH edit, no
# registry change, nothing outside this folder.
/.toolchain
# Scratch for build probes and crash-injection fixtures. In-repo, per CLAUDE.md's
# "no temp files outside the workspace" rule, but never committed.
/.tmp
/demo/out

# The shell is a separate workspace with its own build directory (D-116).
/shell/target/

# autonomous build loop output
.logs/
